@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] compact-presentation-only
Diagnostic classification MUST NOT modify build results, exit status, scheduling,
cancellation or state in another invocation. Completion MUST use the actual Nix
process result, never a word match or application severity.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:logging] compact-capture-before-filter
Every received diagnostic and builder line MUST be archived before console
filtering. The archive MUST preserve original payload bytes, stable physical-line
identifiers and available activity identity. Capture failure MUST be announced and
restore visible logging; a session without a completion record is incomplete.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:capacity] compact-output-budgets
Automatic diagnostic output MUST be bounded to 12 KiB per invocation and 4 KiB
per excerpt, with at most 20 preceding and 20 following lines per build activity.
For a terminal builder failure without an earlier detected error, the excerpt
MAY instead include its last 40 lines within the same byte limit.
Completion has a separate 2 KiB allowance. Progress MUST be at most 160 bytes per
15 seconds. Overlapping context MUST NOT be reprinted. Saved logs retain omitted
output; reaching a presentation budget MUST NOT stop the build.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:logging] compact-structured-precedence
Recognized structured severity MUST take precedence over words in its payload.
Elixir severity, Rust tracing level and Cargo compiler-message message.level MUST
be interpreted through their respective schemas. Text matches are candidates,
never assertions that a build failed. Malformed input MUST NOT stop the build.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] compact-private-evidence
Session logs MUST be private to the invoking user and MUST NOT be automatically
exported to remote logging services. Session metadata MUST NOT record command
arguments or environment values. Existing producer-side diagnostic sanitization
MUST remain effective. Retention MUST NOT delete active sessions.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:compatibility] compact-cli-compatibility
Machine-readable stdout, explicit log formats and an explicit full-output mode
MUST retain their existing semantics. The implementation MUST be compiled into
the pinned Nix executable, not substituted by a shell or subprocess wrapper.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:capacity] compact-bounded-reader
The log reader MUST default to at most 100 lines and 8 KiB, preserve original
line identifiers under filters, and identify the first unreturned record when
truncated. Complete output requires explicit selection. An index is optional and
MUST NOT be required to recover records from an intact archive.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:logging] compact-confidence-priority
Low-confidence word matches and their context MUST consume at most 4 KiB of the
12 KiB diagnostic budget, leaving capacity for structured, recognized textual
and native errors. Classification priority MUST NOT affect archival capture.
